    "sentence_translations": [
      "Who knows more about Chinese culture?",
      "",
      "In the beginning of February, British Prime Minister Theresa May and her husband visited China.",
      "In a news photo, they are seen smiling and holding paper cuttings of the character “happiness” turned upside down.",
      "The English media started to mock them upon seeing this photo, claiming the couple didn’t understand the characters.",
      "Since they were holding the “happiness” character upside down, they had run out of luck.",
      "",
      "Chinese netizens started to laugh when they saw this news.",
      "They said English media is the one who doesn't know about Chinese culture.",
      "In China, people like to put up the “happiness” character upside down, ..",
      ".. because “happiness reversed” sounds the same as “happiness arrived”.",
      "People hope happiness will arrive during the upcoming year.",
      ""
